1. To install PICUT on your Pi Pico you need to install CircuitPython. Get the files here: https://circuitpython.org/downloads
2. Stake out the Pi.
3. Hold the button on the Pi.
4. While you hold the button, insert the cable back in the Pi.
5. Now Copy the recently downloaded file onto the Pi.
6. For QWERTY Layout download following Files out of this repo: config.txt; Setup_EN.py and code_en.py
6.1. Also you´ll need the bundle for your circuitpython version from this side: https://circuitpython.org/libraries
6.2. Unzip the folder and copy from folder lib the folder adafruit_hid onto the folder lib on the Pi.
7. Put Setup_EN.py in an extra folder.
8. Start setup.py as a Programm
8.1 For any People, who dont want to use the Pytho-script, there is also a Setup-Tool writen in Java!
9. Follow the Instructions.
10. Copy the files config.txt and code_en.py onto the Pi.
11. Restart the Pi.
12. Done!
